<gpx version="1.1" creator="Claude Bruce Trail planner" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Day 10 (stop 1 of 2) - Devil's Punch Bowl, Oakridge Drive, New Mountain Road</name></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.212998" lon="-79.748956"><name>P Start/finish parking</name><desc>Roadside Parking: On Leslie Dr west of New Mountain Rd, just north of the railway bridge. Free</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.213940" lon="-79.742420"><name>P2 alternative parking</name><desc>Roadside Parking: On Oakridge Dr off Green Rd, south of King St. Free. Joins the route near km 0.8 (0 m walk).</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.211280" lon="-79.754990"><name>P3 alternative parking</name><desc>Devil's Punch Bowl Conservation Area: Enter from Ridge Rd, east of Centennial Parkway. Paid (amount not confirmed). Joins the route near km 3.8 (0 m walk).</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.212767" lon="-79.748384"><name>J1</name><desc>J1: Turn left onto the white-blazed main Bruce Trail, heading east. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off on your right.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.212493" lon="-79.741483"><name>J2</name><desc>J2: Turn sharp left onto the blue-blazed Oakridge Drive Side Trail, heading north-west. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off ahead.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.213925" lon="-79.742340"><name>J3</name><desc>J3: End of the Oakridge Drive Side Trail. There is trailhead parking here (Roadside Parking: On Oakridge Dr off Green Rd, south of King St). Turn around and retrace your steps.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.212007" lon="-79.758814"><name>J4</name><desc>J4: Continue straight onto the blue-blazed Devil's Punch Bowl Side Trail, heading south-west. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off on your right.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.211211" lon="-79.755223"><name>J5</name><desc>J5: End of the Devil's Punch Bowl Side Trail. There is trailhead parking here (Devil's Punch Bowl Conservation Area: Enter from Ridge Rd, east of Centennial Parkway). Turn around and retrace your steps.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
